<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joachim Ernst, Duke of Anhalt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1901">1901</a>–<a href="/years/1947">1947</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joachim Ernst was the last Duke of Anhalt, succeeding as a minor in September 1918. His regent abdicated on his behalf in November 1918 during the German Revolution, and the duchy became the Free State of Anhalt. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> he was arrested by the Soviet authorities and died in a camp at Buchenwald in 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joachim-ernst-duke-of-anhalt.jpg" alt="Joachim Ernst, Duke of Anhalt" width="290" height="419" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A. Hartmann, Hofphotograph, Dessau [Adolf Hartmann (1864–1923)] · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joachim_Ernst_duke_of_Anhalt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
